0..46 Comment "//! Vectors are lists indexed by their length."
47..50 Comment "//!"
51..128 Comment "//! A vector\'s type states its length. A function then states the length that"
129..144 Comment "//! it returns."
145..148 Comment "//!"
149..218 Comment "//! The kind `Nat -> Type` reads the length type before the universe."
219..245 Comment "//! `VNil` stands at zero."
246..290 Comment "//! `VCons` stands one past its tail length."
291..333 Comment "//! A length call evaluates to its result."
334..385 Comment "//! `plus(m, Zero)` therefore stands at length `m`."
386..389 Comment "//!"
390..472 Comment "//! - cites: [Dybjer-1994-inductive_families] — a family whose constructors each"
473..508 Comment "//!   state the index they stand at"
509..591 Comment "//! - see: #3579 — a family\'s argument written as a call converts with its value"
592..670 Comment "//! - see: #3625 — a constructor\'s field written as a call meets a type that"
671..692 Comment "//!   writes the call"
693..771 Comment "//! - see: #3627 — a constructor at a length written as a call that computes"
772..798 Comment "//!   the length it states"
799..849 Comment "//! - see: `../../pathological/data/vectors.gandr`"
850..853 Comment "//!"
854..955 Comment "//! [Dybjer-1994-inductive_families]: https://doi.org/10.1007/BF01211308 \"Dybjer, Inductive families\""
957..994 Comment "// The naturals the lengths count in."
